<>"†
ƒ"Basics Design: Format" represents the physical point of contact with the user; affecting how we receive a design's printed or online information. The book demonstrates how a creative approach to format selection and a careful consideration of presentation space can produce dramatic results within both print and digital media. It examines established format standards and, with the aid of fully-illustrated examples, suggests how thoughtful application of pre-existing models can add an extra dimension to design."Š
‡O Mpoulmpa etan phobera peismatares. Etan apo keinous tous kharakteres pou tha mporousan na sphurelatethoun sto duskolo 15o aiona, ste misonomadike ekeine gonia tes Europes, otan ole e notia arkhegone Rosia, paratemene apo tous prigkepes tes, eikhe eremothei kai eikhe katakaei mekhri to teleutaio khorto, ap' t' asugkrateta moggolika stiphe otan, steremenos ap' to spiti tou ki apo kathe loges stege, o anthropos egine anagkastika ripsokindunos xekhnontas pos uparkhei phobos ston kosmo. Ten panarkhaie eirenike slabike psukhe ten atsalose e phloga tou polemou kai xepedese to kozakiko, auto to platu, to xephreno demiourgema tes rosikes psukhes."‘
O Iban Ilits Gkolobin, anoteros dikastikos leitourgos, zei mia anete, eukhariste kai euprepe zoe -mekhri pou pephtei apo mia skala kai khtupa to pleuro tou. Arkhizei na ekhei enokhleseis pou den lene na upokhoresoun kai exelissontai se pono. Oi giatroi den mporoun na ton boethesoun kai etsi arkhizei mia anapopheukte poreia, kathos e ugeia tou epideinonetai kai odegeitai se enan argo kai epoduno thanato. Mesa se auto to diastema, to epikeimeno telos ton anagkazei na epanexetasei te zoe tou kai na dei to terastio keno tes."
šThe English novelist E.M.Forster and the Greek Alexandrian poet C.P. Cavafy met when Forster was working for the Red Cross in Alexandria during the First World War. Their subsequent correspondence bears witness to a complex relationship and serves as a fascinating testament to Forster's relentless determination to promote Cavafy by bringing out an English translation of his work. The letters also chronicle Cavafy's calculated refusal to comply fully with Forster's plans. The story they tell involves a number of major twentieth century literary personalities-Arnold Toynbee, T.S. Eliot, T.E. Lawrence, and Leonard Woolf all participated in Forster's early translation project. Forster ultimately succeeded in launching Cavafy's reputation in the English-speaking world, setting an important precedent for his present global literary fame. Included are all extant letters, the earliest Cavafy translations by George Valassopoulo (incorporating Cavafy's own authorial emendations), poems by E.M. Forster, archival photographs, and related letters."
›E dekapentakhrone Kathrin Morlant, mia kopela glukia, kalopiste kai phanatike anagnostria muthistorematon, kanei ten prote tes exodo ston kosmo kai zei mia seira apo phantastikous kai pragmatikous kindunous, prota sto kosmiko kai analaphro Mpath kai ustera sto baru kai epibletiko abbaeio tou Northangker. Khare ston adolo kharaktera tes, tis ethikes arkhes tes kai ten kale tes tukhe, tha bgei apo tis peripeteies tes alobete, ekhontas mathei na xekhorizei ten pragmatike zoe apo ta muthistoremata kai te philia apo ten arpaktikoteta.
To "Abbaeio tou Northangker", proto megalo muthistorema tes Tzeen Osten, einai to pio drosero kai khioumoristiko biblio tes. Ksekina san parodia tou "gotthikou" muthistorematos, me mia eroida pou einai o antipodas ton aitherion kai tragikon eroidon, gia na exelikhthei se ena autodunamo kai apolaustiko realistiko muthistorema, apo ekeina pou anoixan to dromo ste "monterna" pezographia." 
The first and only illustrated biography of "The Man in Black", Johnny Cash, the most famous country singer of all time
Cash was a 17-time Grammy winner who sold more than 90 million albums in his lifetime and became an icon of American music in the 20th century. Graphic novelist Reinhard Kleist depicts Johnny Cash's eventful life from his early sessions with Elvis Presley (1956), through the concert in Folsom Prison (1968), his spectacular comeback in the 1990s, and the final years before his death on September 12, 2003.
Already a bestseller and award-winner in Europe, Johnny Cash: I See a Darkness vividly portrays the unpredictable life of a loner, patriot, outlaw, and music rebel, making this unique biography a compelling read for multiple generations of graphic novel and music fans."¡
To mono muthistorema tou Kharolnt Pinter. E monadike eukairia gia osous pisteuoun ston megalutero agglophono theatrographo tou aiona mas na doun akalupto to prosopo tes euaisthesias tou Pinter, protou perikharakothei oristika mesa sten euphuIa tou, ten ainigmatikoteta tou, protou ginei o idios kai to ergo tou ena ainigma me prosopeio to kathemerina dethen asemanto. O Pinter den "exegei", epeide tote tha parembei sto ergo tou theate-anagnoste. Parathetei eikona, drase e apraxia, prokalei (e pagideuei) ton anagnoste na ginei mokhlos. E poiotes kai e entase tes summetokhes tou anagnoste kanei to keimeno tou Pinter mia theatrike e anagnostike apolause polu upselou epipedou, epibrabeuei te noemosune. Phainomenika khoris drase, me asemanto geras, me epikentro mia adrane Oraia Elene, me anatreptikous ruthmous kai agria, kata topous, exermeno to komiko stoikheio. Kato apo ten apnoia ton arkhikon kephalaion, o anagnostes prokaleitai na probalei te dike tou aekhe kataigida. Meta xespaei o tuphonas. (APO TEN PAROUSIASE STO OPISThOPhULLO TOU BIBLIOU)"¤
¡E Ntominik Ori, me to pseudonumo Polin Reaz, sunegrapse ten tolmere, sadomazokhistike Istoria tes O to 1954.To biblio emelle na ginei apo ta pio poludiabasmena erga tes gallikes logotekhnias.E ekdose tou prokalese salo eno exisou diaseme einai kai e kinematographike metaphora tou to 1975."¤
¡Notable for their magnificent, jewel-like color illustrations by Bilibin, these traditional tales include "The Frog Princess," "Vassilissa the Beautiful," and "The White Duck." Though Russian Fairy Talesin the Pantheon Folklore Library is a book for adults, it has sold over 30,000 copies."§

¤
E Irene, kore mias ekkentrikes kai xepesmenes megaloastes, pou ekhei metatrepsei to spiti tes se oiko eugerias, demiourgei me ton Phransisko, gio Ispanon exoriston apo ten epokhe tou emphuliou polemou, mai philike skhese pou ustera apo polles dokimasies ginetai siga-siga phlogeros erotas. Demosiographos, e Irene briskei tukhaia to nema gia ten anakalupse mias apo tis politikes sphages pou aphthonoun sta khronika ton diktaktorion tes Latinikes Amerikes. E bia strephetai tote enantion tes, kai enantion tou Phransisko, epikheirei polles phores na tous aphanisei kai telika tous katadikazei sten exoria, kainourgious exoristous enos neou emphuliou polemou... Pernontas adiakopa apo to phos sto skotadi kai apo ton erota ston tromo, auto to muthistorema zontaneuei dekades prosopa tragika e asteia, apo ten epileptike khoriatopoula pou kanei thaumata os ton stratego-phantasma pou kubernaei te khora apo to upogeio kataphugio tou, apo ton ierea-ergate tes phtokhogeitonias os ton basaniste axiomatiko, apo ton ametanoeto, gero-anarkhiko os ton omophulophilo antistasiako kommote - kai kurios tis axekhastes morphes gunaikon, meteron suzugon kai thugateron, pou kanoun ten Izampel Aliente apo to proto tes ede biblio, To spiti ton pneumaton, ten kat exokhen suggraphea tes moiras ton gunaikon tes Latinikes Amerikes."©
¦Otan etan paron o Gouillompu, e Marian den eikhe matia gia kanenan allon. Otidepote ekane autos etan sosto* otidepote elege etan exupno. Ki ekeinos, apo ten pleura tou, tis bradies pou epaizan khartia sto Park, eklebe ton eauto tou kai olous tous allous gia na ten abantarei. An e bradia etan khoreutike, etan o apokleistikos skhedon kabalieros tes, kai otan anagkazontan na khoristoun gia enan-duo khorous, phrontizan na briskontai dipla kai spania elegan koubenta se opoiondepote allon. E sumperiphora aute, opos einai eunoeto, tous ekane epikentro tes genikes thumedias. Alla ta gelia kai oi koroidies den tous ptoousan, edeikhnan malista na men tous enokhloun sto elakhisto."ª
§To "Abessalom, Abessalom!" einai to enato muthistorema tou Phokner kai protoekdotheke to 1936. Kentrikos tou khoros einai e phantastike periokhe Gionapatopha pou o suggrapheas te khartographei kai ten topothetei sten politeia tou Misisipe, konta sto Oxphornt. E istoria autou tou topou arkhizei ton perasmeno aiona. Ta prosopa kai ta gegonota, paroti einai phantastika, antanakloun entona katastaseis tes amerikanikes zoes."ª	
§	O "Elithios", mazi me tous "Daimonismenous" kai tous "Adelphous Karamazoph", paramenei ena ap' ta kuriarkha erga tou Ntostogiephski. O prigkipas Miskin, enas epileptikos, gurizei apo mia klinike tes Elbetias, opou kapoios giatros ton eikhe phrontisei apo eusplakhnia. Einai orphanos. Ole ki ole e periousia tou ena mpogalaki roukha. Den xerei tipota ap' te zoe. "Bebaiotheka apoluta", tou leei o giatros, "pos eiste ena paidi, delade olotela paidi. Monakha sto mpoi kai sto prosopo moiazete me antra, ma sten anaptuxe, sten psukhe, sto kharaktera, isos isos kai sto mualo, den ekhete enelikiothei kai tha meinete etsi esto ki an zesete exenta khronia".
Auto to paidi ton eikosi exi khronon einai eugeniko, khoris douloprepeia, deilo, kalo ki aploiko. Den ekhei zesei. E, toulakhiston, den ekhei zesei "en drasei". E zoe tou ekhei diabei se esoterikes enateniseis. Ekhei tampourothei exo ap' ta koinonika teikhe, exo ap' ton kosmo tou "duo kai duo kanoun tessera". Ki otan pephtei anamesa s' auton ton kosmo, mesa se toute ten politeia ten katoikemene apo arpages, apateones, philedonous, paliatsous kai methusous, phainetai san pareisaktos. (Apo ten parousiase sto opisthophullo tou bibliou)"­
ª
"O Anarkhikos ton duo Kosmon, ena apo ta oraiotera politika muthistoremata, kai -eutukhos- okhi mono, apotelei mia apo tis spoudaioteres meletes tes Politikes sto khoro tes Epistemonikes Phantasias kai parallela einai mia endiapherousa melete tes exelixes tes skepses enos epistemona. Apo pleuras ideon einai e megiste douleia tes suggrapheos."
- Makes Panorios
"E Le Guin einai uperokhe sto na prokalei tous anagnostes se ena taxidi exo apo to gnosto kosmo ton aistheseon. O phantastikos kosmos tes einai sugkhronos geinos kai katanoetos."
- The Times"°
­O Gouiliam, einai neos, talantoukhos kai philodoxos mousikos. E zoe tou kulaei anamesa sta tzaz klamp kai tis ergatikes polukatoikies tou Londinou, me ena soro apogoeteuseis na ton basanizoun. Ta pragmata duskola tha mporousan na pane kheirotera, ki omos pane... O atukhos Gouliam ginetai o monadikos marturas mias allokotes dolophonias. Me agrio khioumor kai ruthmo pou thumizei tis kaluteres stigmes tes pop mousikes, o Koou, s' auto to diaskedastiko muthistorema (grammeno prin apo to "Ti oraio Pliatsiko") mas kanei na anakalupsoume to Londino ton mousikon, kapritsiozes kores aristokratikon oikogeneion, skotsezes mpargouman kai koukoulophorous nanous phoniades.
<>
(The Guardian)"·
´Diethnos kataxiomeno, me perissotera apo pente ekatommuria antitupa se kuklophoria, to klasiko muthistorema tou Reu Mprantmperu "Pharenait 451" einai mia istoria gia te logokrisia kai tous anthropous pou ten apsephoun -ena biblio exisou epikairo semera me ten epokhe pou protoekdotheke peripou prin apo exenta khronia.
"To sustema etan aplo. Oloi to katalabainan. Ta biblia eprepe na kaoun, mazi me ta spitia opou etan krummena".
O Gkau Montagk etan puronomos kai e douleia tou etan na bazei photia. To apolambane na bazei photia. Epi deka khronia ekane aute ten ergasia kai den ton problematise pote e eukharistese pou eniothe kata tis nukhterines epidromes e e khara tou otan eblepe tis selides na paradidontai stis phloges... Den ton problematize tipote eos otou sunantese ena dekaeptakhrono koritsi pou tou milese gia to parelthon, gia ton kairo pou oi anthropoi den phobontan. Kai katopin sunantese enan kathegete pou tou milese gia to mellon, gia tis meres pou oi anthropoi tha mporoun na skephtontai. Aiphnes, o Gkau Montagk suneidetopoiese ti eprepe na kanei...
E romalea kai poietike proza tou Mprantmperu kai e asunethiste dioratikoteta tou oson aphora tis dunatotetes tes tekhnologias sunduazontai kai sunthetoun mia prophetike aphegese gia ten upodoulose tou dutikou politismou sta mentia, sta narkotika kai ston komphormismo -mia aphegese ephamille tou "1984" tou Orgouel kai tou "Thaumastos kainourgios kosmos" tou Khaxleu.
"Mia istoria pou anastatonei ton anagnoste kathos exereuna to ti sumbainei otan e agnoia -sten pio akraia morphe tes- theoreitai arete".
("The Times")"»
